---
import Article from "@/layouts/article.astro"
import { GITHUB_URL } from "@/lib/links"

const LICENSE_URL = `${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`
---

<Article title="Terms">
  <p>
    Wonnet is open-source software under the{" "}
    <a href={LICENSE_URL}>MIT license</a>, and our server is the service that
    syncs your mail for the apps. By using them you agree to the following.
  </p>

  <h2>Your accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You may only add mail accounts that are yours to use. You are responsible
    for what you send with Wonnet, and for following the terms of your mail
    providers.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair use</h2>
  <p>
    Don't use Wonnet to send spam, to break the law, or to get in the way of the
    service for others. We may suspend accounts that do.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The software and the service are provided as they are, without warranty of
    any kind. Keep your mail with your provider: Wonnet syncs it, it is not a
    backup. We aren't liable for damage or loss that comes from using them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may change the service or these terms. If a change matters, we will say
    so on this page.
  </p>
</Article>
